window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0d13cd021ae98686"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"plan-a-dashboard-and-monitoring-workflow\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">规划仪表盘与监控工作流</h1> <p>明确指标、负责人、质量检查，以及仪表盘所支持的决策。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供策略说明、工作流背景、指标定义、来源数据导出、仪表盘示例和利益相关方反馈，然后请它起草仪表盘规格与监控计划。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>正在制定新仪表盘，或重做已经无法支持决策的仪表盘的团队。</li> <li>需要记录 KPI 层级、图表规格、筛选器和质量检查的指标工作。</li> <li>规划所有权、监控和发布交接的分析师与运营人员。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查仪表盘背后的源数据、指标定义和质量检查。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读策略说明、仪表盘示例和利益相关方反馈。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>编写可编辑的仪表盘规格，并说明负责人、交接事项和发布风险。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>起草仪表盘规格</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请为[workflow, product, or business question]起草一份仪表盘规格。\n\n请使用我提供的策略说明、工作流背景、指标定义、来源数据导出、仪表盘示例和利益相关方反馈。请返回：\n\n- 仪表盘应支持的决策\n- KPI 层级和指标定义\n- 图表和筛选器规格\n- 数据质量与 QA 检查\n- 负责人和交接事项\n- 监控计划\n- 发布与访问风险\n\n不要编造指标；未经来源验证，不要声称仪表盘已可用于生产环境。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：数据科学团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/datasets-and-reports\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">分析数据集并交付报告（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"design-around-decisions-not-charts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">围绕决策设计，而不是围绕图表</h2> <p>编写仪表盘规格前，先明确它要支持哪些决策，以及哪些负责人会根据指标采取行动。向 ChatGPT 提供指标定义、来源数据导出、现有示例、工作流背景和利益相关方反馈，让规格始终建立在真实数据上。</p> <ol> <li>说明工作流、受众、需要做出的决策和审查频率。</li> <li>附上指标词汇表、来源数据导出、仪表盘示例和利益相关方反馈。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 找出来源缺口、质量检查和负责人需求。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，起草 KPI 层级、图表规格、筛选器和监控方案。</li> <li>审查发布风险，并用来源数据测试拟定的指标。</li> </ol> <p>请把仪表盘规格视为分析师、数据负责人和使用者之间的约定。明确每张图表代表什么、何时可以信任它，以及它应该触发什么行动。</p> <p><a id=\"make-monitoring-actionable\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">让监控真正可执行</h2> <p>规格审查通过后，请 ChatGPT 把价值最高的检查项整理成监控清单，并明确升级处理的边界。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this dashboard spec into a monitoring checklist.\n\nFor each KPI, include:\n\n- source and owner\n- expected update cadence\n- freshness and quality checks\n- threshold or anomaly to inspect\n- who should be notified\n- evidence to attach before escalating\n\nKeep the checklist draft-only and do not create alerts or publish the dashboard.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">把这份仪表板规格转成监控检查清单。\n\n为每个 KPI 列出：\n\n- 数据来源和负责人\n- 预期更新频率\n- 数据时效性与质量检查\n- 要检查的阈值或异常\n- 应通知的人\n- 上报升级处理前需要附上的证据\n\n这份清单只保留为草稿，不要创建告警或发布仪表板。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"plan-a-dashboard-and-monitoring-workflow\">Plan a dashboard and monitoring workflow</h1> <p>Define metrics, owners, quality checks, and the decisions a dashboard supports.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT a strategy brief, workflow context, metric definitions, source exports, dashboard examples, and stakeholder feedback, then ask it to draft a dashboard spec and monitoring plan.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams defining a new dashboard or rebuilding one that no longer supports decisions.</li> <li>Metrics work that needs KPI hierarchy, chart specs, filters, and quality checks documented.</li> <li>Analysts and operators planning ownership, monitoring, and publication handoffs.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect source data, metric definitions, and quality checks behind the dashboard.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read strategy briefs, dashboard examples, and stakeholder feedback.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Produce an editable dashboard spec with owners, handoffs, and publication risks.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Draft the dashboard spec</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Draft a dashboard specification for [workflow, product, or business question].\n\nUse the strategy brief, workflow context, metric definitions, source exports, dashboard examples, and stakeholder feedback I provide. Return:\n\n- the decisions the dashboard should support\n- KPI hierarchy and metric definitions\n- chart and filter specifications\n- data-quality and QA checks\n- owners and handoffs\n- monitoring plan\n- publication and access risks\n\nDo not invent metrics or claim that a dashboard is production-ready without validating its sources.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Data science teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/datasets-and-reports\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Analyze datasets and ship reports (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"design-around-decisions-not-charts\">Design around decisions, not charts</h2> <p>Before specifying a dashboard, define the decisions it should support and the owners who will act on the signals. Give ChatGPT metric definitions, source exports, existing examples, workflow context, and stakeholder feedback so the spec stays grounded in actual data.</p> <ol> <li>Name the workflow, audience, decisions, and review cadence.</li> <li>Attach the metric glossary, source exports, dashboard examples, and stakeholder feedback.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to identify source gaps, quality checks, and ownership needs.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt to draft KPI hierarchy, chart specs, filters, and monitoring.</li> <li>Review the publication risks and test the proposed metrics against source data.</li> </ol> <p>Treat the dashboard spec as a contract between analysts, data owners, and users. Define what each chart means, when it should be trusted, and what action it should trigger.</p> <h2 id=\"make-monitoring-actionable\">Make monitoring actionable</h2> <p>After the spec is reviewed, ask ChatGPT to turn the highest-value checks into a monitoring checklist with clear escalation boundaries.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this dashboard spec into a monitoring checklist.\n\nFor each KPI, include:\n\n- source and owner\n- expected update cadence\n- freshness and quality checks\n- threshold or anomaly to inspect\n- who should be notified\n- evidence to attach before escalating\n\nKeep the checklist draft-only and do not create alerts or publish the dashboard.\n</code></pre>"};
